Customer Churn Prediction — Machine Learning

Author: Shoaib Muhammad
Internship: Neurofive Solutions — Machine Learning Track
Task: Customer Churn Prediction
Dataset: Telco Customer Churn

Project Overview

Customer churn prediction is a practical machine learning problem used by organizations to identify customers who are likely to leave a service. Early identification of high-risk customers can help businesses design targeted retention strategies and reduce customer loss.

This project analyzes the Telco Customer Churn dataset and develops two classification models:

Decision Tree Classifier

Logistic Regression

The project covers data cleaning, exploratory data analysis (EDA), preprocessing, model training, performance evaluation, feature importance analysis, and business interpretation.

Objectives

Explore factors associated with customer churn.

Clean and preprocess the dataset.

Handle categorical and numerical variables.

Identify class imbalance.

Train a Decision Tree Classifier.

Train a Logistic Regression model.

Compare model performance.

Identify the top three predictive features.

Translate findings into business insights.

Dataset

The dataset contains 7,043 customers and 21 columns.

Important variables include:

tenure — Number of months the customer has stayed

MonthlyCharges — Monthly service charges

TotalCharges — Total amount charged

Contract — Contract type

InternetService — Internet service type

PaymentMethod — Payment method

Churn — Target variable

Target Variable

No → Customer stayed

Yes → Customer churned

Data Preprocessing

The following steps were performed:

Inspected dataset structure and data types.

Checked missing values.

Converted TotalCharges to numeric.

Removed rows with missing values after conversion.

Checked for duplicate records.

Removed customerID.

Converted Churn to binary values (No = 0, Yes = 1).

Applied One-Hot Encoding to categorical variables.

Applied Standard Scaling to numerical variables.

Used a stratified 80/20 train-test split.

Exploratory Data Analysis

Key Findings

Overall churn rate: 26.58%

Month-to-month churn rate: 42.71%

One-year contract churn rate: 11.28%

Two-year contract churn rate: 2.85%

Average tenure of churned customers: 17.98 months

Average tenure of retained customers: 37.65 months

Average monthly charges for churned customers: 74.44

Average monthly charges for retained customers: 61.31

Fiber-optic churn rate: 41.89%

Electronic-check churn rate: 45.29%

Class Imbalance

Class

Percentage

No Churn

