Note: Feature importance represents predictive importance within the trained Decision Tree. It does not prove direct causation.

Business Summary

The analysis found that 26.58% of customers churned, with churn strongly associated with contract type, tenure, and customer charges. Month-to-month customers showed substantially higher churn than customers with one-year or two-year contracts. Logistic Regression achieved the best overall test performance with 80.38% accuracy and 83.59% ROC-AUC, while the Decision Tree provided slightly higher churn recall. The Decision Tree identified month-to-month contracts, fiber-optic internet service, and total charges as its three most important predictive features. These findings can help businesses identify higher-risk customers and develop targeted retention strategies.

