Conclusion

This project demonstrates an end-to-end customer churn prediction workflow, including data exploration, data cleaning, preprocessing, model training, evaluation, feature analysis, and business interpretation.

The results show that machine learning can provide useful signals for identifying customers at higher risk of churn. In this experiment, Logistic Regression performed best overall, while the Decision Tree provided valuable interpretability and feature-importance insights.

Future improvements could include hyperparameter tuning, class-weight optimization, threshold adjustment, cross-validation, and more advanced churn prediction models.

